## Summary

The public SDK changes valid exact observation keys and values before returning them. Following `nextRequest` and feeding its returned key/value into `observe` can leave hypotheses unresolved or eliminate the very hypothesis whose predicted value was selected.

Reproduced on PR #1 at `a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb`, package version `2026.10.25`, Node `24.22.1`, and the pinned `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.24`. Only a fresh synthetic filesystem tracker was used.

## Minimal SDK reproduction

Save as `repro.ts` at that checkout's root and run `node repro.ts` with its dependencies available:

```ts
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { mkdtemp, rm } from 'node:fs/promises';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';
import { open, add, nextRequest, observe, matrix } from './index.ts';

const root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'hypothesis-roundtrip-'));
try {
  const workspace = join(root, '.agents', 'pm');
  const client = new PmClient({ pmRoot: workspace, author: 'fixture', noExtensions: true });
  await client.init('hyp', { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip', mergeFence: false });
  const options = { workspace, author: 'fixture' };
  const { investigation } = await open('Synthetic latency incident', options);
  const a = await add(investigation, 'Below threshold',
    [{ observation: 'latency', value: '<500ms' }], options);
  await add(investigation, 'Above threshold',
    [{ observation: 'latency', value: '>500ms' }], options);
  const request = (await nextRequest(investigation, options)).request!;
  const selected = request.groups.find(g => g.hypotheses.includes(a.hypothesis))!;
  await observe(investigation, request.observation, selected.value, options);
  const result = await matrix(investigation, options);
  console.log({ selected: selected.value, statuses: result.rows.map(r => r.status) });
  assert.equal(result.rows.find(r => r.id === a.hypothesis)!.status, 'viable');
} finally {
  await rm(root, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
```

Expected: the selected value is the original `<500ms`; the matching hypothesis is viable and the alternative is eliminated.

Actual: the selected value contains a literal backslash-u escape, `\\u003c500ms`. Both hypotheses are eliminated because that value equals neither original prediction.

An independent key-only case also fails: predictions on `latency<500ms` return the key `latency\\u003c500ms`. Observing that returned key leaves both hypotheses unknown, since the new fact targets a different key.

## Cause and impact

[`nextRequest`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/hypothesis.ts#L76-L80) calls `safe` before returning structured data. [`safe` and `inert`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/core.ts#L19-L21) replace characters inside strings rather than applying an output serialization escape. [`matrix` and `resumePacket`](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/blob/a7ff9519c4b7155859d331a9f79fd6b41749dafb/src/hypothesis.ts#L71-L92) use the same transformation.

The transformation is also non-injective: a real `<` and the literal six-character string `\\u003c` produce the same returned text. A caller cannot reliably repair this by decoding escapes. This affects machine consumers and copied CLI values, not the underlying equality comparison, which correctly compares the changed observation against the original data.

## Acceptance

- Returned observation keys and predicted values can be passed unchanged from `nextRequest` into `observe`.
- Matrix/resume machine-readable fields preserve exact values or expose an unambiguous lossless representation.
- Distinguish real controls/markup from literal backslash-u sequences.
- Keep terminal rendering inert at the presentation boundary rather than changing SDK data semantics.
- Add round-trip regression coverage for keys and values containing `<`, `>`, backticks, newline/control characters, and literal escape strings.

Canonical owner: [pm-hypothesis PR #1](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-hypothesis/pull/1). The fault occurs in this package before the host SDK receives the observation. This is a focused correctness reproduction, not a full release or remote-backend certification.



